# Curriculum Overview

## What is AI and Algorithmic Decisions all about?
 
#### In **AI and Algorithmic Decisions**, students take the next step as developers, transforming their web pages into interactive apps with **JavaScript**. 

#### Acting as front-end developers, they learn how algorithms and conditional logic drive user interactions. 

#### With AI as a coding coach and debugging partner, students plan app behavior with flowcharts, write and refine code, and build confidence through problem-solving and iteration.

---

#### ***Note: Unlike the first semester, the second semester of AI Foundations is a continuous sequence and must be taught in order. AI and Algorithmic Decisions is the 2nd unit in the course.***

## Student Learning Goals
<div style="display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; background: #f7f8fa; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 4px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1); font-size: 14pt; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 800px; margin: 20px auto;">

  <div>
    <h4 style="margin-top: 0; font-weight: bold;">By the end of this unit, students will be able to :</h4>
    <ul style="list-style-type: disc; padding-left: 10px; font-size: 14pt">
      <li>Model user interactions as algorithms and translate them into JavaScript code using event-driven programming.

</li> <br>
      <li>Design and interpret flowcharts to plan program logic and structure app behavior.</li><br>
      <li>Write, organize, and debug JavaScript code using variables, functions, and if/else statements.
</li><br>
      <li>Use AI tools as supportive partners for debugging, reflection, and learning new coding strategies.
</li><br>
<li>Evaluate the role of AI in coding, demonstrating accountability for the quality and ethics of their own code.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <img src="https://images.code.org/6478f46b5bbaa8fc6468c40a545f9994-image-1760978656971.png" 
         alt="Icon with computer and weblayout" 
